2. Python runtime dependencies — NOT bundled
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The plugin does not ship Python wheels. The user's interpreter must satisfy:

  mcp>=1.27,<2          MIT
  pydantic>=2           MIT
  jsonschema>=4.20,<5   MIT
  pywin32>=305          PSF-2.0
  comtypes>=1.2.0       MIT
  httpx                 BSD-3-Clause        (mcp transport dependency)
  ezdxf, numpy, Pillow, lxml, openpyxl, python-docx, python-pptx, XlsxWriter
                        (only for the DFM / DXF / FEA / report families)

License identifiers above are the upstream projects' declared licenses as of
2026-10-29; they are listed for operator information, not as a redistribution
claim, because nothing here is redistributed. A distributor that bundles a
Python environment must re-verify each license and ship the corresponding texts.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. SolidWorks and Microsoft COM
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SolidWorks is commercial software from Dassault Systèmes, not distributed here.
The user must own and license a local SolidWorks installation. This plugin
invokes it through the registered COM automation interface only.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. No code from the dsh-solidworks (AGPL) repository
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This package contains no source code from the separate `dsh-solidworks`
repository. Policy tiers, one-shot grants, path gating, the stdio MCP client,
the host entry point, CLI, tests, and documentation were written for this
package. See PROVENANCE.md for the line-level comparison that supports this.